<para>Offset of sector or facet integration variable records from beginning of data vector in local variable storage associated with an element</para>
<para>Function used only if index refers to a sector- or facet integration point variable.</para>
<para>Method takes offset calculated in property database ignoring the number of integration points because these will vary from element to element type. This offset is now expanded for the element variable of interest by multiplicating those other element integration point variables which precede the current variable.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="attention"><para>storage order is: all sector integration point variables for the first ip, then the second and so forth. Subsequently all facet integration point variables in the same fashion.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para>: this method is only used for the reading of variables that are stored in the LVS associated with <ref refid="classcsmp_1_1_element" kindref="compound">Element</ref> objects</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="attention"><para><ref refid="structcsmp_1_1_index_1a74a6be7459ba4a62d9bf33c311918178" kindref="member">Index::offsetFactorSector</ref> is zero for sector integration point variables and 1 for facet integration point variables </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
